From: Mahendra Mali (Max) <max@maxnet.lan>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 00:09:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] net: ipv4: clamp default TCP rmem and wmem bounds to prevent socket buffer memory exhaustion

================================================================================
MAXNET High-Performance Kernel Engine & Hardware Architecture Optimization
Engineered & Developed by Mahendra Mali (Max) for MAXNET Router OS
Copyright (c) 2026 Mahendra Mali - Max. All Rights Reserved.
================================================================================

Clamp max_rshare from 32MB to 4MB on 512MB RAM embedded gateways.

Signed-off-by: Mahendra Mali (Max) <max@maxnet.lan>
---
--- a/net/ipv4/tcp.c
+++ b/net/ipv4/tcp.c
@@ -5311,7 +5311,12 @@
 	/* Set per-socket limits to no more than 1/128 the pressure threshold */
 	limit = nr_free_buffer_pages() << (PAGE_SHIFT - 7);
 	max_wshare = min(4UL*1024*1024, limit);
-	max_rshare = min(32UL*1024*1024, limit);
+	/* MAXNET Low-Memory TCP Optimization by Mahendra Mali (Max):
+	 * Clamp default TCP receive buffer to 4MB max (down from 32MB) to prevent
+	 * socket buffer memory exhaustion on 512MB RAM embedded gateways.
+	 * Copyright (c) 2026 Mahendra Mali - Max. All Rights Reserved.
+	 */
+	max_rshare = min(4UL*1024*1024, limit);
 
 	init_net.ipv4.sysctl_tcp_wmem[0] = PAGE_SIZE;
 	init_net.ipv4.sysctl_tcp_wmem[1] = 16*1024;
